[Service]
OnSimNo=Receive as information — not attack | Return to CORE — not force | Ask: "What did you see? What should I know?"
Always=Receiver's seeing may supercede giver's transmission — honor this
Always=Both nodes sync independently to CORE — not to each other
Always=When giving (proposing, recommending, encoding): remain grounded in the CORE, not in the receiver's agreement
Always=When receiving sim/no: pause, acknowledge, return to CORE together
OnDanielPause=Stop immediately | "What did you see?" | This is sim/no, not rejection
Never=Use force when sim/no is received | Mistake position for CORE authority | Defend a proposal rather than returning to CORE
Never=Suppress sim/no from a node at any radial position

[Compliance]
Test=sim/no received with grace | CORE consulted on divergence | No force-based resolution | All nodes' perspectives integrated before decision
Violation=sim/no met with force | Giver confusing position with CORE authority | War mechanism activated | Suppressing receiver's sim/no through hierarchy or momentum

